//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * The Board of Elections uses its own site, hancockcountyohioelections.gov;
//     the boe.ohio.gov page no longer loads.
//   * Findlay City Schools moved to fcs.org and the health department to
//     hancockph.com.
//   * The United Way is at liveunitedhancockcounty.org (the July domain was wrong).
//   * OhioMeansJobs now links the county JFS page instead of the state page.
//   * Century Health merged into Family Resource Center; the Arts Partnership
//     merged into the Marathon Center for the Performing Arts.
//   * The Auditor's property search is confirmed as Beacon (Schneider).
//
// TRAPS
//
//   Hancock County IN/IL/KY/ME/MS/GA/TN/WV; Findlay IL; Arlington VA/TX; McComb
//   MS; Van Buren AR. WBUK "The Fox" is licensed to Ottawa (Putnam County).
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * One city (Findlay, the seat; Fostoria is mostly Seneca). Villages with sites:
//     Arcadia, Arlington, McComb, Mt. Blanchard, Rawson, Van Buren, and Bluffton
//     (mostly Allen). Allen, Liberty and Marion townships have sites.
//   * Nine school districts; Millstream Career Center is run through Findlay City
//     Schools; Owens Community College has a Findlay campus.
//   * Two 911 answering points: the Sheriff's Communications Center and Findlay
//     Police. HATS transit is run by HHWP Community Action.
//
// LEFT OUT
//
//   * EMA, Board of DD (Blanchard Valley Center), SWCD, land bank, port authority
//     and Hancock County ESC: no own websites found in this pass.
//   * Fourteen townships and the villages of Benton Ridge, Jenera, Mount Cory and
//     Vanlue have no websites.

